## Resolution

Added complete supported-graph vector-Jacobian products and transactional SGD parameter updates, accumulating every branch/use into one gradient per shared object. All five gated representations, affine layers, activations and additions have independently checked full-graph gradients. Logical training buffers, model batches/activations and configured forward-row work are checked before computation.

Added versioned regression data/run/training-record/report formats and CLI entries `train-regression`, `check-experiment`, `replay-regression`. Samples have explicit predeclared splits and related groups; duplicate IDs, cross-split groups and exact input duplicates are refused. Full-batch SGD uses train only, chooses the earliest minimum-validation-MSE checkpoint including epoch zero and evaluates test after selection. Complete input/data/config/history/provenance and the selected standalone model are saved without overwrites. Replay restarts a run, not an optimizer checkpoint. Existing model format schemas are unchanged; SGD provenance is bound through its new training record rather than mislabeled as manual replacement history.

At `f76c8376`, **52 Rust host tests**, both portable release rlibs, numerical/QSL/model regressions and the complete training/check/replay CLI cycle passed on the NRL branch. PyTorch checks every full-graph gradient and one SGD step; central differences check all 271 trainable values and nine inputs independently. All 129 regression history entries and the selected model match the external oracle. Validation selected epoch **91 of 128**; on this synthetic task test MSE changed from **0.7019184889255535** to **0.016083866958995992**. Changing test targets cannot change selected parameters or epoch. All three fixture files regenerate byte-identically. The dated report records the exact tested configuration and limitations.

[Evidence](../nrl/reports/regression-training-2026-10-26.json), [raw log](../nrl/reports/training-check-2026-10-26.txt), [saved replayable experiment](../nrl/reports/regression-example-2026-10-26/report.json), [contract](../nrl/specs/regression-v0.md). The initial/selected models, full data/config and actual Rust history are saved alongside the example report.

T05 now has its first complete independent non-language regression profile. Parent 900 remains open for language/classification, local calibration/distillation, optimizer resume, evaluation/benchmark comparison, mixed-plan/search, measured optimization and native execution. The full repository gate and main integration belong to the deferred landing round; no speed, compression, pretrained-model or native guarantee follows from this synthetic task.
